{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004274-2e-tremere-as-ordo-dracul-and-mekhet-bloodline","id":1004274,"title":"[2E] Tremere as Ordo Dracul and Mekhet Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T23:53:51-08:00","id":1004274,"title":"[2E] Tremere as Ordo Dracul and Mekhet Bloodline","content":"A year back I made some interesting idea how to recreate Masquarad Tremere Clan as both Mekhet Bloodline <b><i>and </i></b>Ordo Dracul secret faction. Here is sum up of this idea:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=581992#post581992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More thinking of Tremere vampires in new World of Darkness, I would make them <b>both</b> Ordo Dracul secret faction and Mekhet Bloodline. From the Mage <b>Left Hand Path, </b> Tremere Liches lore says they were slaves to Theban that made some mages in to Breath-Eaters - vampires surviving by breath, not blood.<br /> <br /> As this, I would make those that survived the massacre by Liches to finally be freed from Theban slavery and become Mekhet Bloodline with special Discipline of Blood usage ( maybe called <i>Sanguine</i>, or something ), with final power of surviving on Breath, not Blood - five different powers per Discipline in <b>Requiem</b> 2ED are still a thing? I would give them some power over Blood Bonds, Blood usage and finally, on living on Breath of victims. They were see as threat to some Kindred from similarities of they powers to those of the Strix and their feeding habits.<br /> <br /> Our Tremere Bloodline would gone in to secrecy by centuries, developing more and more Blood Sorcery they stolen from Theban ( <b><i>not</i></b> their Disicpilne ) and when Ordo Dracul come to being, they infiltrated it and make a large secret faction in Dragons secret society. Now, Tremere Kindred are Ordo Dracul that practice their Blood Sorcery and have very antagonistic views on Lancea et Sanctum ( and probably Invictus ) - but, mainly, they want to dwell in to mages society to uncover Tremere Liches and plan, after centuries in hiding, to take care Awakened soul-eating parasites that almost killed the millenia before. They are Ordo's faction dedicated to contacts with mages, inflirtrating Orders in secret to uncover Tremere Liches in them.<br /> <br /> They do not feel to me as whole Covenant, or that different from Ordo Dracul to make them really new Covenant onto itself. They will work better now as faction admits the Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>So with <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">new sheets from <b>Mr Gone</b> with Man &amp; Beast archetypes</a>, I wanted to write up vampire Prince of London, from my <b>Mage</b> chronicle I run in there. I know I want him to be from Tremere faction in Ordo ( maybe from the Bloodline, but don't think so ), but still cannot decide on (Requiem) Clan of him.<b> Maybe you can help me with deciding what particular Clan members would do and be like in Tremere/Ordo faction? </b>Some examples would be great.<br /> <br /> Also, I want to make in this topic fan Mekhet Bloodline I wrote above - if it does not is prepared before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T08:20:16-08:00","id":1004436,"title":"","content":"Ok, this is an interesting project. And one that I think has good potential lead to some final, balanced codifying of Tremere in VtR. There's been some thoughts on the Tremere as a covenant or Ordo Dracul before, but I haven't seen anything solid. Just &quot;this is a likely representation.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Disclaimer: I'm no expert on the Tremere and don't have my books in front of me.)<br /> <br /> First, here are some of my impressions of Tremere Blood Thaumaturgy, from VtM, mixed with CoD: it's based on Hermetic principles and essentially represents codified Paths of specific effects that a true mage would find easier to do with their Spheres. Rituals are pure blood-magic, of the sort that mortal hedge mages could do at lesser effectiveness and much greater difficulty. It gets around paradox by being rigid and drawing on vitae as the magic energy fuel.<br /> <br /> For the Ordo Dracul, this would be an interesting line of investigation in so much as it posits a fundamental link between Kindred disciplines, blood sorcery and true magic. The magician, at a base level, understands that magic is energy+will+intellect directed toward a specific effect. Since vampires are sustained by life-energy condensed into vitae, a magical effect by itself, an Ordo faction could easily view Blood Thaumaturgy as a coil.<br /> <br /> In fact (From whitewolf wiki):<ul><li>The <b>Palatine Rite</b>, a rite centered around Middle Europe that focuses on the study of dark arts (namely Blood Sorcery) and is vehemently opposed to the Circle of the Crone.</li> </ul><br /> So the Tremere would fit within the Palatine, or as a new Rite--and as a Faction. How you mechanically represent Blood Thaumaturgy is something I'm interested in: is it one coil with scales as the rituals? Are the paths merits? VtR 2e seems to be avoiding adding new Disciplines through bloodlines, and stacking stuff into various forms of merits instead.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like recycling VtM material into headcanon if it makes sense and furthers the story. So, examples? From the original inner circle?<br /> <br /> <b>LeDuc</b> [Mekhet], devoted to the investigation of the secrets of magic, particularly through intense observation and voluminous writing and research. Frequently sent to uncover magical tidbits from true mages as well as digging through the ancient history of vampiric clans and their own blood sorcery. <br /> <br /> <b>Goratrix</b> [Nosferatu], devoted to the investigation of how magical energies react to the vampiric body and how the sympathy of mind affects it with the will. His methods encompass all manner of mutilation and sacrific--self and others, and he quails not at terrorizing entire legions of subservient mortals, slaves and organizations to dance in the sympathetic patterns he needs. <br /> <br /> <b>Etrius</b> [Ventrue], devoted to the investigation of the will and how power and control leads to effect; this is as much external as internal as he acts as leadership of the Tremere and the marshaling (and mentoring) of its members toward their common goals--a natural position for a natural leader and the best magician.<br /> <br /> <b>Calderon</b> [Daeva], devoted to understanding how magic effects the mortal world and how that bends back to affect the intellect and will. While not as focused or effective a thaumaturge, his role is just as vital in that he uses his extensive mortal contacts and subtle influence to acquire reagents, resources and unique blood. <br /> <br /> <b>Meerlinda</b> [Gangrel], devoted to understanding where magic comes from and how it flows within the world, and thence into the blood. She sees thaumaturgy as a natural extension of older forms of magic--geomancy, astrology, sacrificial traditions and the like; she likes to stylize herself as channeling the wisdom and sagacity of the ancients, but the veneer is notoriously thin. <br /> <br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}